{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"bhy3t6dxy","task_type":"local_bash","description":"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3_repair_1\ncat > hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nRefinement of the incumbent `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`: people still find a sequence less random when one stretch of it shows a striking local heads/tails excess, still compare its switching rate with their own ideal (with their own sensitivity, judging switching too often more leniently than too rarely by a shared fraction), and still use personal weights on overall imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry and run-length variety, and a personal guessing rate. The one change is that a departure from one's ideal switching rate is weighed as evidence that grows (or shrinks) with the number of flip-to-flip transitions it is observed over — a shared power of sequence length — so the same off-ideal switching rate is shrugged off in a short sequence and taken seriously in a long one (or the reverse, if the fitted exponent is negative), while the streak, balance, symmetry and local-excess cues keep their length-blind weights; this predicts that the alternation preference is weaker for short pairs and stronger for long pairs than the incumbent's length-blind ideal-rate penalty implies.\nEOF\necho length_weighted_ideal_rate_lopsided > model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\np='candidate.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\"\"\"Personal leniency toward over-alternation, on top of the most lopsided stretch.\n\nRefinement of `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`: one striking local\nheads/tails excess still makes a sequence look designed, on top of the personal\nideal switching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the\nlongest run, shared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry and run-length\nvariety, and a personal lapse rate; switching more than one's ideal still costs\na fraction of what the same shortfall costs. The one change: that fraction is\neach person's own trait, drawn from a population, instead of shared.\n\"\"\"''','''\"\"\"Length-weighted evidence from the ideal switching rate, with the most lopsided stretch.\n\nRefinement of `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`: one striking local\nheads/tails excess still makes a sequence look designed, on top of the personal\nideal switching rate and sensitivity (over-alternation judged leniently by a\nshared fraction), personal weights on imbalance and the longest run, shared\nweights on the final run, mirror symmetry and run-length variety, and a\npersonal lapse rate. The one change: a departure from one's ideal switching\nrate counts as evidence that scales with a shared power of the number of\ntransitions it is observed over, so the same off-ideal rate matters more (or\nless) in a long sequence than in a short one; the other cues stay length-blind.\n\"\"\"''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"lopsided_b\": lopsided_stretch(b),\n    }''','''        \"lopsided_b\": lopsided_stretch(b),\n        \"n_trans\": (len(a) - 1) / 7.0,\n    }''')\ns=s.replace('''    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\"''','''    n_trans = pm.Data(\"n_trans\", np.ones(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\"''')\ns=s.replace('''    # Personal fraction of the ideal-rate penalty applied to over-alternation\n    # (non-centred log-normal population).\n    mu_over = pm.Normal(\"mu_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_over = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_over\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_over = pm.Normal(\"z_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    over_frac = pm.math.exp(mu_over + sigma_over * z_over)\n''','''    # Shared fraction of the ideal-rate penalty applied to over-alternation.\n    log_over = pm.Normal(\"log_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    over_frac = pm.Deterministic(\"over_frac\", pm.math.exp(log_over))\n\n    # Shared exponent: how the ideal-rate evidence scales with the number of\n    # transitions (0: length-blind; positive: long sequences weigh it more).\n    tau = pm.Normal(\"tau\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    length_weight = pt.power(n_trans, tau)\n''')\ns=s.replace('''    o = over_frac[participant_id]\n''','')\ns=s.replace(\"pt.switch(dev > 0, o, 1.0)\",\"pt.switch(dev > 0, over_frac, 1.0)\")\ns=s.replace(\"score_a = -b * rate_penalty\",\"score_a = -b * length_weight * rate_penalty\")\ns=s.replace(\"score_b = -b * rate_penalty\",\"score_b = -b * length_weight * rate_penalty\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"length_weight\\|over_frac\\|n_trans\" candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && time /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3_repair_1 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"}],"uuid":"5b632a31-5d3c-4849-be41-333f0c8972f3","session_id":"aa679723-f8de-4e4d-b765-6cba7da9f661"}
