{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdLzySq8gJAihAWKLYwz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote all three files for the repair slot, and the self-check passes with `OK`. I haven't checked novelty against the incumbent, because the check doesn't test it. If the length exponent comes out near zero, this model could again predict like the incumbent and be rejected as a near-duplicate.\n\n**What I changed.** The first attempt's change (making leniency toward over-alternation a personal trait) barely moved the average predictions, so it scored as a near-duplicate (RMSE 0.0018, under the 0.002 cutoff). I dropped it and made a different change to the incumbent, `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`, that varies across stimuli:\n\n- **Hypothesis:** how far a sequence's switching rate is from a person's ideal now counts as evidence that grows (or shrinks) with how many transitions the sequence has. One shared exponent on sequence length sets this, and it is fitted from the data.\n- **Prediction:** short pairs are judged less by alternation, and long pairs more, than the incumbent's length-blind penalty implies. If the fitted exponent is negative, it's the other way round.\n- **What stays the same:** the lenient treatment of over-alternation (one shared fraction again), the lopsided-stretch cue and all the other cues, which still ignore length.\n- **Name:** `length_weighted_ideal_rate_lopsided`.\n\n**Self-check result.** The model loads, has a finite log-probability, meets the data contract and finished the short test fit. Its ELPD-LOO there was -3498.7, against the incumbent's -3500.3, but that's one 100-draw chain, not a real comparison. The same short fit flagged the PSIS-LOO estimate as unreliable (7.8% of trials above the Pareto-k limit). Convergence, speed and the reliability of the estimate will only be settled by admission's full fit. The test fit took about 2.5 minutes of sampling on one CPU, well within the 30-minute limit.\n\nThis is the second and final attempt for this slot, so any rejection stands.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3_repair_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689,"cache_read_input_tokens":89964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":689,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa679723-f8de-4e4d-b765-6cba7da9f661","uuid":"58005c9a-8f1e-412b-931a-2bfb1f2d49ff","timestamp":"2026-10-02T11:39:14.162Z","request_id":"req_011CfdLzxt6e5ecoCuhEJL5H"}
